# Auto-resolve merge conflicts on documentation-table files where two parallel
# feature branches append independent rows. `merge=union` keeps both sides'
# additions, which is the right semantic for table rows — the parallel
# modules genuinely want both rows preserved.
#
# Intentionally NOT auto-resolved here (routed to the /resolve_merge_conflict
# agent in adw_ship_iso.py instead):
#   - Python registry files (api/v1/__init__.py, models/__init__.py,
#     core/response_codes.py). Union is a dumb text merge and can produce
#     silently-duplicated imports or `v1_router.include_router(X)` calls
#     that py_compile does not catch (Python tolerates duplicate imports;
#     FastAPI raises only at registration time on path collision).
#   - TypeScript config arrays (adminNav.ts, routes.ts). TS files get no
#     fast post-merge validation, so union-produced duplicates would slip
#     past until next build.
#
# The agent's /resolve_merge_conflict spec explicitly dedupes identifiers
# during its append-only-union strategy, which is the safety the dumb
# `merge=union` driver lacks.

.claude/commands/conditional_docs.md merge=union
